## Gmail parser
Commit `9aed16d` implemented semantic classification and was pushed.

Classification:
1. OTP → NON_TRANSACTION
2. Due reminder → NON_TRANSACTION
3. Anchor-free promotional email → NON_TRANSACTION
4. Credit-card payment received → transfer
5. Refund → refund
6. debited/spent/paid → expense
7. credited/received → income, LOW confidence + review
8. direction-neutral amount → UNKNOWN
9. unanchored currency amount → UNKNOWN
10. otherwise UNKNOWN

OTP, due reminders and promotions are excluded. Credit-card payments cannot become income. Refund/transfer are distinct.

Message ID is identity; thread ID is never used.

Real Gmail has NOT been scanned yet. Mock tests passed.

Known real-data risks to evaluate during the eventual read-only scan:
- multiple anchors/amounts in one email may expose fixed anchor-priority behavior;
- HTML-only templates may need better extraction.

